-- Tests for the exceptions group: Chapter 4 (ss 76-95) and Chapter 4A
-- (ss 96-106A) of the Penal Code 1871, and the roll-up in pc-exceptions.l4.
--
-- Expected values come FROM THE SOURCE: each Illustration is cited on the line
-- above its assertion (`-- s 79 illus (b)`); an Explanation applied as a test
-- is cited the same way. Variants that are not Illustrations say which words of
-- the section decide them. A failing assertion here is a finding, not a typo.
--
-- The fixtures spell every field of their record (L4 has no record update), so
-- each lists all leaves with the ones the Illustration establishes set TRUE.
-- (They were expanded from a short template by a script that reads the field
-- lists out of the DECLAREs and rejects a misspelt field; this file is the
-- source of record and may be edited by hand.)
--
-- The POLARITY property (FORK E-1): for every exception, the all-FALSE record -
-- what the charge generator sends when nothing is known - gives FALSE. That is
-- Evidence Act 1893 s 107's "the court is to presume the absence of such
-- circumstances", asserted once per exported ladder in the last section.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-exceptions-general`
IMPORT `pc-exceptions-private-defence`
IMPORT `pc-exceptions`

§ `Chapter 4 - tests`

§§ `s 76`

-- s 76 illus (a): a soldier fires on a mob by the order of his superior
-- officer, in conformity with the commands of the law. No offence.
`a soldier firing on a mob by lawful order` MEANS `Bound or Justified by Law Facts` WITH
    `bound by law to do it` IS TRUE
    `justified by law in doing it` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `exception under s 76` `a soldier firing on a mob by lawful order`

-- s 76 illus (b): A forcefully seizes Z, who is stabbing Y to death on a
-- public road, to detain him for the police, under the power the law gives to
-- all persons apprehending murderers in the act. No offence.
`seizing a murderer in the act` MEANS `Bound or Justified by Law Facts` WITH
    `bound by law to do it` IS FALSE
    `justified by law in doing it` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 76` `seizing a murderer in the act`

-- s 6 illus (b): a police officer, without warrant, apprehends Z, who has
-- committed murder; he was bound by law to apprehend Z. Not wrongful confinement.
`a police officer apprehending a murderer` MEANS `Bound or Justified by Law Facts` WITH
    `bound by law to do it` IS TRUE
    `justified by law in doing it` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `exception under s 76` `a police officer apprehending a murderer`

§§ `s 77`

`a judge acting judicially under a power he believes in good faith he has` MEANS `Judicial Act Facts` WITH
    `done by a judge` IS TRUE
    `acting judicially` IS TRUE
    `in the exercise of a power which is given to him by law` IS FALSE
    `in the exercise of a power which in good faith he believes to be given to him by law` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 77` `a judge acting judicially under a power he believes in good faith he has`

-- "when acting judicially": a judge not so acting is outside s 77.
`a judge not acting judicially` MEANS `Judicial Act Facts` WITH
    `done by a judge` IS TRUE
    `acting judicially` IS FALSE
    `in the exercise of a power which is given to him by law` IS FALSE
    `in the exercise of a power which in good faith he believes to be given to him by law` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 77` `a judge not acting judicially`

§§ `s 78`

-- "notwithstanding the court may have had no jurisdiction ..., provided the
-- person doing the act in good faith believes that the court had such
-- jurisdiction"
`executing an order of a court without jurisdiction, believing in good faith it had jurisdiction` MEANS `Court Order Facts` WITH
    `done in pursuance of the judgment or order of a court of justice` IS TRUE
    `warranted by the judgment or order of a court of justice` IS FALSE
    `done while the judgment or order remains in force` IS TRUE
    `the person doing the act in good faith believes that the court had such jurisdiction` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 78` `executing an order of a court without jurisdiction, believing in good faith it had jurisdiction`

-- "if done while the judgment or order remains in force"
`executing an order no longer in force` MEANS `Court Order Facts` WITH
    `done in pursuance of the judgment or order of a court of justice` IS TRUE
    `warranted by the judgment or order of a court of justice` IS FALSE
    `done while the judgment or order remains in force` IS FALSE
    `the person doing the act in good faith believes that the court had such jurisdiction` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 78` `executing an order no longer in force`

§§ `s 79`

-- s 79 illus (a): A seizes Z, whom he sees commit what appears to be a
-- murder, to bring him before the authorities; Z may have acted in
-- self-defence. No offence.
`seizing an apparent murderer` MEANS `Mistake of Fact Facts` WITH
    `no written law provides otherwise` IS TRUE
    `by reason of a mistake of fact or in ignorance of a fact` IS TRUE
    `in good faith believes himself to be bound by law to do it` IS FALSE
    `in good faith believes himself to be justified by law in doing it` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 79` `seizing an apparent murderer`

-- s 79 illus (b): a police officer screening passengers shoots Z, who shouts
-- he has a bomb and runs; Z had no bomb. No offence.
`the airport shooting` MEANS `Mistake of Fact Facts` WITH
    `no written law provides otherwise` IS TRUE
    `by reason of a mistake of fact or in ignorance of a fact` IS TRUE
    `in good faith believes himself to be bound by law to do it` IS FALSE
    `in good faith believes himself to be justified by law in doing it` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 79` `the airport shooting`

-- s 79 illus (c): a police officer on patrol shoots Z, who fits a bomber's
-- profile and runs towards a crowd. No offence.
`the train station shooting` MEANS `Mistake of Fact Facts` WITH
    `no written law provides otherwise` IS TRUE
    `by reason of a mistake of fact or in ignorance of a fact` IS TRUE
    `in good faith believes himself to be bound by law to do it` IS FALSE
    `in good faith believes himself to be justified by law in doing it` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 79` `the train station shooting`

-- s 79 illus (d): a naval commander orders fire on vessel A, believing it is
-- about to ram a cruise liner. No offence.
`the naval commander` MEANS `Mistake of Fact Facts` WITH
    `no written law provides otherwise` IS TRUE
    `by reason of a mistake of fact or in ignorance of a fact` IS TRUE
    `in good faith believes himself to be bound by law to do it` IS FALSE
    `in good faith believes himself to be justified by law in doing it` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 79` `the naval commander`

-- s 79 illus (e): an officer of a court, ordered to arrest Y, after due
-- enquiry arrests Z believing him to be Y. No offence.
`arresting the wrong man under a court's order` MEANS `Mistake of Fact Facts` WITH
    `no written law provides otherwise` IS TRUE
    `by reason of a mistake of fact or in ignorance of a fact` IS TRUE
    `in good faith believes himself to be bound by law to do it` IS TRUE
    `in good faith believes himself to be justified by law in doing it` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `exception under s 79` `arresting the wrong man under a court's order`

-- "Unless otherwise provided by written law"
`a mistake where written law excludes the defence` MEANS `Mistake of Fact Facts` WITH
    `no written law provides otherwise` IS FALSE
    `by reason of a mistake of fact or in ignorance of a fact` IS TRUE
    `in good faith believes himself to be bound by law to do it` IS TRUE
    `in good faith believes himself to be justified by law in doing it` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 79` `a mistake where written law excludes the defence`

-- "in good faith" (s 26B): a belief formed without due care and attention.
`a careless belief` MEANS `Mistake of Fact Facts` WITH
    `no written law provides otherwise` IS TRUE
    `by reason of a mistake of fact or in ignorance of a fact` IS TRUE
    `in good faith believes himself to be bound by law to do it` IS FALSE
    `in good faith believes himself to be justified by law in doing it` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 79` `a careless belief`

§§ `s 79A`

`a mistake of law, with no written law making it a defence` MEANS `Mistake of Law Facts` WITH
    `mistake of law or ignorance of the law` IS TRUE
    `a written law provides that it is a defence` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `mistake of law is a defence under s 79A` `a mistake of law, with no written law making it a defence`

`a mistake of law that a written law makes a defence` MEANS `Mistake of Law Facts` WITH
    `mistake of law or ignorance of the law` IS TRUE
    `a written law provides that it is a defence` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `mistake of law is a defence under s 79A` `a mistake of law that a written law makes a defence`

§§ `s 80`

-- s 80 illus (a): the hatchet head flies off and kills a bystander; "if there
-- was no want of proper caution on the part of A, his act is excusable".
`the flying hatchet head` MEANS `Accident Facts` WITH
    `done by accident or misfortune` IS TRUE
    `in the doing of a lawful act` IS TRUE
    `in a lawful manner` IS TRUE
    `by lawful means` IS TRUE
    `with proper care and caution` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 80` `the flying hatchet head`

-- ... and, with a want of proper caution, it is not.
`the flying hatchet head, carelessly` MEANS `Accident Facts` WITH
    `done by accident or misfortune` IS TRUE
    `in the doing of a lawful act` IS TRUE
    `in a lawful manner` IS TRUE
    `by lawful means` IS TRUE
    `with proper care and caution` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 80` `the flying hatchet head, carelessly`

§§ `s 81`

-- s 81 illus (a): the steamer captain alters course to avoid boat B (20-30
-- passengers), knowing he may run down boat C (2 passengers), without intending
-- to; not guilty "if it be found as a matter of fact that the danger ... was
-- such as to excuse him".
`the steamer captain` MEANS `Necessity Facts` WITH
    `an offence, if at all, merely by reason of its being done with the knowledge that it is likely to cause harm` IS TRUE
    `done in good faith for the purpose of preventing or avoiding other harm to person or property` IS TRUE
    `the harm to be prevented or avoided was of such a nature and so imminent as to justify or excuse the risk` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 81` `the steamer captain`

-- ... and if the danger is found NOT to be such as to excuse him, he is not
-- within the exception (the Explanation).
`the steamer captain, the danger not excusing the risk` MEANS `Necessity Facts` WITH
    `an offence, if at all, merely by reason of its being done with the knowledge that it is likely to cause harm` IS TRUE
    `done in good faith for the purpose of preventing or avoiding other harm to person or property` IS TRUE
    `the harm to be prevented or avoided was of such a nature and so imminent as to justify or excuse the risk` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 81` `the steamer captain, the danger not excusing the risk`

-- ... "if A alters his course without any intention to run down the boat C":
-- with that intention, the offence is not "merely by reason of" knowledge.
`the steamer captain, intending to run down boat C` MEANS `Necessity Facts` WITH
    `an offence, if at all, merely by reason of its being done with the knowledge that it is likely to cause harm` IS FALSE
    `done in good faith for the purpose of preventing or avoiding other harm to person or property` IS TRUE
    `the harm to be prevented or avoided was of such a nature and so imminent as to justify or excuse the risk` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 81` `the steamer captain, intending to run down boat C`

-- s 81 illus (b): pulling down houses in a great fire to stop it spreading,
-- in good faith, to save life or property.
`pulling down houses in a great fire` MEANS `Necessity Facts` WITH
    `an offence, if at all, merely by reason of its being done with the knowledge that it is likely to cause harm` IS TRUE
    `done in good faith for the purpose of preventing or avoiding other harm to person or property` IS TRUE
    `the harm to be prevented or avoided was of such a nature and so imminent as to justify or excuse the risk` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 81` `pulling down houses in a great fire`

-- s 81 illus (c): the naval commander disables hijacked vessel A to protect
-- about 100 people at the ferry terminal.
`disabling the hijacked vessel` MEANS `Necessity Facts` WITH
    `an offence, if at all, merely by reason of its being done with the knowledge that it is likely to cause harm` IS TRUE
    `done in good faith for the purpose of preventing or avoiding other harm to person or property` IS TRUE
    `the harm to be prevented or avoided was of such a nature and so imminent as to justify or excuse the risk` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 81` `disabling the hijacked vessel`

§§ `ss 82 and 83`

#ASSERT `below 10 years of age` 9
#ASSERT NOT `below 10 years of age` 10
#ASSERT NOT `of or above 10 years and below 12 years of age` 9
#ASSERT `of or above 10 years and below 12 years of age` 10
#ASSERT `of or above 10 years and below 12 years of age` 11
#ASSERT NOT `of or above 10 years and below 12 years of age` 12

-- s 6 illus (a): definitions are understood subject to "nothing shall be an
-- offence which is done by a child below 10 years of age".
`a child of 9` MEANS `Child Facts` WITH
    `the child is below 10 years of age` IS `below 10 years of age` 9
    `the child is of or above 10 years and below 12 years of age` IS `of or above 10 years and below 12 years of age` 9
    `has not attained sufficient maturity of understanding to judge of the nature and consequence of his conduct on that occasion` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `exception under s 82` `a child of 9`
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 83` `a child of 9`

`a child of 11 without sufficient maturity of understanding` MEANS `Child Facts` WITH
    `the child is below 10 years of age` IS `below 10 years of age` 11
    `the child is of or above 10 years and below 12 years of age` IS `of or above 10 years and below 12 years of age` 11
    `has not attained sufficient maturity of understanding to judge of the nature and consequence of his conduct on that occasion` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 83` `a child of 11 without sufficient maturity of understanding`
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 82` `a child of 11 without sufficient maturity of understanding`

`a child of 11 with sufficient maturity of understanding` MEANS `Child Facts` WITH
    `the child is below 10 years of age` IS `below 10 years of age` 11
    `the child is of or above 10 years and below 12 years of age` IS `of or above 10 years and below 12 years of age` 11
    `has not attained sufficient maturity of understanding to judge of the nature and consequence of his conduct on that occasion` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 83` `a child of 11 with sufficient maturity of understanding`

`a person of 12 without sufficient maturity of understanding` MEANS `Child Facts` WITH
    `the child is below 10 years of age` IS `below 10 years of age` 12
    `the child is of or above 10 years and below 12 years of age` IS `of or above 10 years and below 12 years of age` 12
    `has not attained sufficient maturity of understanding to judge of the nature and consequence of his conduct on that occasion` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 83` `a person of 12 without sufficient maturity of understanding`

§§ `s 84`

-- s 84 illus: A, under a delusion of divine instruction, believes it morally
-- right to kill Z, but knows it is contrary to law. The defence is not
-- available.
`the divine instruction delusion` MEANS `Unsoundness of Mind Facts` WITH
    `at the time of doing it, by reason of unsoundness of mind` IS TRUE
    `incapable of knowing the nature of the act` IS FALSE
    `incapable of knowing that his act is wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS TRUE
    `incapable of knowing that his act is wrong as contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `completely deprived of any power to control his actions` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 84` `the divine instruction delusion`

-- s 84(1)(b) read with (2): incapable of knowing BOTH.
`incapable of knowing the act wrong in either sense` MEANS `Unsoundness of Mind Facts` WITH
    `at the time of doing it, by reason of unsoundness of mind` IS TRUE
    `incapable of knowing the nature of the act` IS FALSE
    `incapable of knowing that his act is wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS TRUE
    `incapable of knowing that his act is wrong as contrary to law` IS TRUE
    `completely deprived of any power to control his actions` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `exception under s 84` `incapable of knowing the act wrong in either sense`

-- s 84(1)(a) and (c), each alone.
`incapable of knowing the nature of the act` MEANS `Unsoundness of Mind Facts` WITH
    `at the time of doing it, by reason of unsoundness of mind` IS TRUE
    `incapable of knowing the nature of the act` IS TRUE
    `incapable of knowing that his act is wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `incapable of knowing that his act is wrong as contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `completely deprived of any power to control his actions` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `exception under s 84` `incapable of knowing the nature of the act`

`completely deprived of power to control his actions` MEANS `Unsoundness of Mind Facts` WITH
    `at the time of doing it, by reason of unsoundness of mind` IS TRUE
    `incapable of knowing the nature of the act` IS FALSE
    `incapable of knowing that his act is wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `incapable of knowing that his act is wrong as contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `completely deprived of any power to control his actions` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 84` `completely deprived of power to control his actions`

-- "by reason of unsoundness of mind": an incapacity from another cause.
`incapable of knowing the nature of the act, but not by reason of unsoundness of mind` MEANS `Unsoundness of Mind Facts` WITH
    `at the time of doing it, by reason of unsoundness of mind` IS FALSE
    `incapable of knowing the nature of the act` IS TRUE
    `incapable of knowing that his act is wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `incapable of knowing that his act is wrong as contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `completely deprived of any power to control his actions` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 84` `incapable of knowing the nature of the act, but not by reason of unsoundness of mind`

§§ `ss 85 and 86`

-- s 85(2)(a): spiked, and did not know what he was doing.
`spiked drink, did not know what he was doing` MEANS `Intoxication Facts` WITH
    `by reason of the intoxication did not know what he was doing` IS TRUE
    `by reason of the intoxication did not know that the act was wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `by reason of the intoxication did not know that the act was wrong as contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `the state of intoxication was caused without his knowledge or against his will` IS TRUE
    `by reason of the intoxication was of unsound mind as determined in accordance with section 84` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `exception under s 85` `spiked drink, did not know what he was doing`
#ASSERT `the effect under s 86(1)` `spiked drink, did not know what he was doing` EQUALS `the accused person must be acquitted`

-- s 85(2): the same, but he got drunk of his own will.
`voluntary drunkenness, did not know what he was doing` MEANS `Intoxication Facts` WITH
    `by reason of the intoxication did not know what he was doing` IS TRUE
    `by reason of the intoxication did not know that the act was wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `by reason of the intoxication did not know that the act was wrong as contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `the state of intoxication was caused without his knowledge or against his will` IS FALSE
    `by reason of the intoxication was of unsound mind as determined in accordance with section 84` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 85` `voluntary drunkenness, did not know what he was doing`
#ASSERT `the effect under s 86(1)` `voluntary drunkenness, did not know what he was doing` EQUALS `section 86(1) has nothing to say, the defence under section 85 not being established`

-- s 85(2)(b) read with (2A): knowing the act contrary to law defeats limb (b).
`spiked, thought it morally right but knew it unlawful` MEANS `Intoxication Facts` WITH
    `by reason of the intoxication did not know what he was doing` IS FALSE
    `by reason of the intoxication did not know that the act was wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS TRUE
    `by reason of the intoxication did not know that the act was wrong as contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `the state of intoxication was caused without his knowledge or against his will` IS TRUE
    `by reason of the intoxication was of unsound mind as determined in accordance with section 84` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 85` `spiked, thought it morally right but knew it unlawful`

-- s 85(3), and s 86(1)'s exception: of unsound mind by reason of intoxication,
-- however it came about.
`drug-induced psychosis` MEANS `Intoxication Facts` WITH
    `by reason of the intoxication did not know what he was doing` IS FALSE
    `by reason of the intoxication did not know that the act was wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `by reason of the intoxication did not know that the act was wrong as contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `the state of intoxication was caused without his knowledge or against his will` IS FALSE
    `by reason of the intoxication was of unsound mind as determined in accordance with section 84` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 85` `drug-induced psychosis`
#ASSERT `the effect under s 86(1)` `drug-induced psychosis` EQUALS `section 84 of this Code and sections 251 and 252 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 apply`

§§ `ss 87, 88, 89 and 91`

#ASSERT `above 18 years of age` 19
#ASSERT `above 18 years of age` 18
#ASSERT NOT `above 18 years of age` 17
#ASSERT `below 12 years of age` 11
#ASSERT NOT `below 12 years of age` 12

-- s 87 illus: A and Z fence for amusement; the agreement implies consent to
-- harm caused without foul play; A, playing fairly, hurts Z. No offence.
`fencing for amusement` MEANS `Consent to Harm Facts` WITH
    `not intended to cause death` IS TRUE
    `not intended to cause grievous hurt` IS TRUE
    `not known by the doer to be likely to cause death or grievous hurt` IS TRUE
    `the person harmed is above 18 years of age` IS `above 18 years of age` 30
    `has given consent, whether express or implied, to suffer that harm` IS TRUE
    `has consented to take the risk of that harm` IS FALSE
    `the harm is harm which the doer knew the act to be likely to cause` IS FALSE
    `done in good faith for the benefit of the person harmed` IS FALSE
    `the person harmed is below 12 years of age` IS FALSE
    `the person harmed is of unsound mind` IS FALSE
    `done by, or by the consent of, the guardian or other person having lawful charge of that person` IS FALSE
    `not the intentional causing of death, or the attempting to cause death` IS FALSE
    `not the doing of anything which the doer knows to be likely to cause death` IS FALSE
    `not the voluntary causing of grievous hurt, or the attempting to cause grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of preventing death or grievous hurt, or curing a grievous disease or infirmity` IS FALSE
    `not the abetment of an offence to which the exception would not extend` IS FALSE
    `not an offence independently of any harm to the person giving the consent, or on whose behalf it is given` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 87` `fencing for amusement`

-- s 87: "to any person above 18 years of age".
`fencing for amusement with a boy of 17` MEANS `Consent to Harm Facts` WITH
    `not intended to cause death` IS TRUE
    `not intended to cause grievous hurt` IS TRUE
    `not known by the doer to be likely to cause death or grievous hurt` IS TRUE
    `the person harmed is above 18 years of age` IS `above 18 years of age` 17
    `has given consent, whether express or implied, to suffer that harm` IS TRUE
    `has consented to take the risk of that harm` IS FALSE
    `the harm is harm which the doer knew the act to be likely to cause` IS FALSE
    `done in good faith for the benefit of the person harmed` IS FALSE
    `the person harmed is below 12 years of age` IS FALSE
    `the person harmed is of unsound mind` IS FALSE
    `done by, or by the consent of, the guardian or other person having lawful charge of that person` IS FALSE
    `not the intentional causing of death, or the attempting to cause death` IS FALSE
    `not the doing of anything which the doer knows to be likely to cause death` IS FALSE
    `not the voluntary causing of grievous hurt, or the attempting to cause grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of preventing death or grievous hurt, or curing a grievous disease or infirmity` IS FALSE
    `not the abetment of an offence to which the exception would not extend` IS FALSE
    `not an offence independently of any harm to the person giving the consent, or on whose behalf it is given` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 87` `fencing for amusement with a boy of 17`

-- s 88 illus: a surgeon, knowing an operation is likely to cause Z's death,
-- not intending it, and intending in good faith Z's benefit, operates with Z's
-- consent. No offence.
`the risky operation with consent` MEANS `Consent to Harm Facts` WITH
    `not intended to cause death` IS TRUE
    `not intended to cause grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `not known by the doer to be likely to cause death or grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `the person harmed is above 18 years of age` IS FALSE
    `has given consent, whether express or implied, to suffer that harm` IS TRUE
    `has consented to take the risk of that harm` IS TRUE
    `the harm is harm which the doer knew the act to be likely to cause` IS FALSE
    `done in good faith for the benefit of the person harmed` IS TRUE
    `the person harmed is below 12 years of age` IS FALSE
    `the person harmed is of unsound mind` IS FALSE
    `done by, or by the consent of, the guardian or other person having lawful charge of that person` IS FALSE
    `not the intentional causing of death, or the attempting to cause death` IS FALSE
    `not the doing of anything which the doer knows to be likely to cause death` IS FALSE
    `not the voluntary causing of grievous hurt, or the attempting to cause grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of preventing death or grievous hurt, or curing a grievous disease or infirmity` IS FALSE
    `not the abetment of an offence to which the exception would not extend` IS FALSE
    `not an offence independently of any harm to the person giving the consent, or on whose behalf it is given` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 88` `the risky operation with consent`
-- ... and it is NOT within s 87, because the surgeon knew death likely.
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 87` `the risky operation with consent`

-- s 89 illus: A, in good faith, for the benefit of his child below 12, has
-- the child cut for the stone by a surgeon, without the child's consent,
-- knowing it likely to cause death but not intending it; the object was the
-- cure. A is within the exception.
`cutting a child for the stone` MEANS `Consent to Harm Facts` WITH
    `not intended to cause death` IS FALSE
    `not intended to cause grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `not known by the doer to be likely to cause death or grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `the person harmed is above 18 years of age` IS FALSE
    `has given consent, whether express or implied, to suffer that harm` IS FALSE
    `has consented to take the risk of that harm` IS FALSE
    `the harm is harm which the doer knew the act to be likely to cause` IS FALSE
    `done in good faith for the benefit of the person harmed` IS TRUE
    `the person harmed is below 12 years of age` IS `below 12 years of age` 8
    `the person harmed is of unsound mind` IS FALSE
    `done by, or by the consent of, the guardian or other person having lawful charge of that person` IS TRUE
    `not the intentional causing of death, or the attempting to cause death` IS TRUE
    `not the doing of anything which the doer knows to be likely to cause death` IS FALSE
    `not the voluntary causing of grievous hurt, or the attempting to cause grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of preventing death or grievous hurt, or curing a grievous disease or infirmity` IS TRUE
    `not the abetment of an offence to which the exception would not extend` IS TRUE
    `not an offence independently of any harm to the person giving the consent, or on whose behalf it is given` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `exception under s 89` `cutting a child for the stone`

-- s 89 proviso (b): knowing death likely, for a purpose OTHER than preventing
-- death or grievous hurt or curing a grievous disease.
`a dangerous act on a child, not to cure` MEANS `Consent to Harm Facts` WITH
    `not intended to cause death` IS FALSE
    `not intended to cause grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `not known by the doer to be likely to cause death or grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `the person harmed is above 18 years of age` IS FALSE
    `has given consent, whether express or implied, to suffer that harm` IS FALSE
    `has consented to take the risk of that harm` IS FALSE
    `the harm is harm which the doer knew the act to be likely to cause` IS FALSE
    `done in good faith for the benefit of the person harmed` IS TRUE
    `the person harmed is below 12 years of age` IS `below 12 years of age` 8
    `the person harmed is of unsound mind` IS FALSE
    `done by, or by the consent of, the guardian or other person having lawful charge of that person` IS TRUE
    `not the intentional causing of death, or the attempting to cause death` IS TRUE
    `not the doing of anything which the doer knows to be likely to cause death` IS FALSE
    `not the voluntary causing of grievous hurt, or the attempting to cause grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of preventing death or grievous hurt, or curing a grievous disease or infirmity` IS FALSE
    `not the abetment of an offence to which the exception would not extend` IS TRUE
    `not an offence independently of any harm to the person giving the consent, or on whose behalf it is given` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 89` `a dangerous act on a child, not to cure`

-- s 89 proviso (a): the intentional causing of death is never within it.
`intentionally causing a child's death` MEANS `Consent to Harm Facts` WITH
    `not intended to cause death` IS FALSE
    `not intended to cause grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `not known by the doer to be likely to cause death or grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `the person harmed is above 18 years of age` IS FALSE
    `has given consent, whether express or implied, to suffer that harm` IS FALSE
    `has consented to take the risk of that harm` IS FALSE
    `the harm is harm which the doer knew the act to be likely to cause` IS FALSE
    `done in good faith for the benefit of the person harmed` IS TRUE
    `the person harmed is below 12 years of age` IS `below 12 years of age` 8
    `the person harmed is of unsound mind` IS FALSE
    `done by, or by the consent of, the guardian or other person having lawful charge of that person` IS TRUE
    `not the intentional causing of death, or the attempting to cause death` IS FALSE
    `not the doing of anything which the doer knows to be likely to cause death` IS FALSE
    `not the voluntary causing of grievous hurt, or the attempting to cause grievous hurt` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of preventing death or grievous hurt, or curing a grievous disease or infirmity` IS TRUE
    `not the abetment of an offence to which the exception would not extend` IS TRUE
    `not an offence independently of any harm to the person giving the consent, or on whose behalf it is given` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `exception under s 89` `intentionally causing a child's death`

-- s 91 illus: causing miscarriage (unless authorised under the Termination of
