§ `The roll-up, and ss 26G(5) and 301(2)`

`nothing established - Bound or Justified by Law Facts` MEANS `Bound or Justified by Law Facts` WITH
    `bound by law to do it` IS FALSE
    `justified by law in doing it` IS FALSE
`nothing established - Judicial Act Facts` MEANS `Judicial Act Facts` WITH
    `done by a judge` IS FALSE
    `acting judicially` IS FALSE
    `in the exercise of a power which is given to him by law` IS FALSE
    `in the exercise of a power which in good faith he believes to be given to him by law` IS FALSE
`nothing established - Court Order Facts` MEANS `Court Order Facts` WITH
    `done in pursuance of the judgment or order of a court of justice` IS FALSE
    `warranted by the judgment or order of a court of justice` IS FALSE
    `done while the judgment or order remains in force` IS FALSE
    `the person doing the act in good faith believes that the court had such jurisdiction` IS FALSE
`nothing established - Mistake of Fact Facts` MEANS `Mistake of Fact Facts` WITH
    `no written law provides otherwise` IS FALSE
    `by reason of a mistake of fact or in ignorance of a fact` IS FALSE
    `in good faith believes himself to be bound by law to do it` IS FALSE
    `in good faith believes himself to be justified by law in doing it` IS FALSE
`nothing established - Mistake of Law Facts` MEANS `Mistake of Law Facts` WITH
    `mistake of law or ignorance of the law` IS FALSE
    `a written law provides that it is a defence` IS FALSE
`nothing established - Accident Facts` MEANS `Accident Facts` WITH
    `done by accident or misfortune` IS FALSE
    `in the doing of a lawful act` IS FALSE
    `in a lawful manner` IS FALSE
    `by lawful means` IS FALSE
    `with proper care and caution` IS FALSE
`nothing established - Necessity Facts` MEANS `Necessity Facts` WITH
    `an offence, if at all, merely by reason of its being done with the knowledge that it is likely to cause harm` IS FALSE
    `done in good faith for the purpose of preventing or avoiding other harm to person or property` IS FALSE
    `the harm to be prevented or avoided was of such a nature and so imminent as to justify or excuse the risk` IS FALSE
`nothing established - Child Facts` MEANS `Child Facts` WITH
    `the child is below 10 years of age` IS FALSE
    `the child is of or above 10 years and below 12 years of age` IS FALSE
