-- s 26G(5): A throws a stone at B in private defence; it hits C, against whom
-- A had no right. A may rely on the defence as though the stone had hit B.
`a stone thrown at an assailant in private defence strikes a bystander` MEANS `Transferred Defence Facts` WITH
    `a defence or exception in law applies as the act or effect actually was` IS FALSE
    `the physical elements of the offence included the doing of an act or the causing of an effect concerning a person or thing` IS TRUE
    `the accused person believed or intended that the act or effect would concern a different person or thing` IS TRUE
    `a defence or exception in law would apply had the act or effect concerned the person or thing the accused person believed or intended it to concern` IS TRUE
    `the accused person, by doing anything which he intends or knows to be likely to cause death, commits culpable homicide by causing the death of a person whose death he neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause` IS FALSE
    `a defence or exception in law would apply had he caused the death of the person whose death he intended or knew himself to be likely to cause` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `the accused person may rely on a defence under section 26G(5)` `a stone thrown at an assailant in private defence strikes a bystander`
#ASSERT `a defence or exception in law is available to the accused person` `a stone thrown at an assailant in private defence strikes a bystander`

-- s 301(2): A shoots at B in private defence and kills C.
`a shot at an assailant in private defence kills a bystander` MEANS `Transferred Defence Facts` WITH
    `a defence or exception in law applies as the act or effect actually was` IS FALSE
    `the physical elements of the offence included the doing of an act or the causing of an effect concerning a person or thing` IS FALSE
    `the accused person believed or intended that the act or effect would concern a different person or thing` IS FALSE
    `a defence or exception in law would apply had the act or effect concerned the person or thing the accused person believed or intended it to concern` IS FALSE
    `the accused person, by doing anything which he intends or knows to be likely to cause death, commits culpable homicide by causing the death of a person whose death he neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause` IS TRUE
    `a defence or exception in law would apply had he caused the death of the person whose death he intended or knew himself to be likely to cause` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `the accused person may rely on a defence under section 301(2)` `a shot at an assailant in private defence kills a bystander`
#ASSERT `a defence or exception in law is available to the accused person` `a shot at an assailant in private defence kills a bystander`
#ASSERT NOT `the accused person may rely on a defence under section 26G(5)` `a shot at an assailant in private defence kills a bystander`

